message: "If you use CausalSieve in research, engineering, or benchmarks, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "CausalSieve: Zero-Dependency SIMD Online Multivariate Causal Discovery, Exogenous Root-Cause Localization, and Lossless-Recoverable Stream Digests"
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: "2026-11-22"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/pgg898200-ship-it/causalsieve"
url: "https://pgg898200-ship-it.github.io/causalsieve/"
authors:
  - name: "CausalSieve Contributors"
keywords:
  - causal-discovery
  - granger-causality
  - root-cause-analysis
  - streaming-time-series
  - lingam
  - e-process
  - simd
  - mcp
abstract: >-
  CausalSieve is a zero-runtime-dependency C++20 SIMD and Python streaming
  engine for online multivariate causal discovery, precision-whitened exogenous
  root-cause localization, exact Block-Schur conditional Granger causality,
  online non-Gaussian contemporaneous orientation, anytime-valid Ville
  E-process alarms, counterfactual do-interventions, and 95-99.95%
  token-compressed stream digests with bit-exact FP64 slice recovery.
